v1.0.12 — the email subject becomes the app's signature

'a note' was a placeholder I never decided. Replaced with the chosen line:

    Sotto Voce - A Song Shared Between Us

Every note now carries the same subject, and that is deliberate. Gmail threads
matching subjects, so every note she sends lands in ONE conversation — which is
exactly what 7c calls the shelf: "a song shared between us, in fragments." One
thread is the feature, not a side effect.

Note the casing: the in-app mark stays lowercase italic (sotto voce, a score
marking on paper). The subject is Title Case because it is a signature read in a
mail inbox. Different context, different job. Both are intentional.

Gate caught a real leak on the way in: the explanatory comment named a person.
Removed. check.sh fails the build on that, and it worked.

Verified: decoded subject is byte-identical to the chosen line, recipient address
still unencoded, zero Google calls, no console errors.
